        {
          "name": "fault_irq",
          "direction": "output",
          "width": 1
        }
      ],
      "functionality": "Implements the complete control/safety shell around a host-provided command workflow. Decodes firmware MMIO accesses to control/configuration/status registers. Accepts streamed compact command words, checks sequence freshness, command age/timeout, range and slew limits, updates shadow registers on accepted commands, emits a response word describing accept/reject and applied command, and drives a clamped actuator command only when a command is accepted. Sticky fault bits report stale, timeout, range-violation, sequence-error, and fallback-inhibited conditions. The design never performs surrogate inference or CFD and never exposes large payload interfaces.",
      "responsibilities": [
        "Provide a firmware-visible control/status register map.",
        "Provide a compact command input stream and response output stream.",
        "Validate sequence number monotonicity, freshness, and timeout conditions.",
        "Clamp requested actuator values to configured min/max bounds.",
        "Apply slew-rate limiting relative to the last applied command.",
        "Maintain shadow state for last accepted command, last applied command, fault code, heartbeat timestamp, and sequence tracking.",
        "Assert fault interrupt/event on stale, timeout, invalid, or inhibited commands.",
        "Drive a bounded actuator command output only when a command is valid and accepted."
      ],
      "must_drive": [
        "host_reg_ready",
        "host_reg_rdata",
        "host_reg_rvalid",
        "host_reg_error",
        "cmd_stream_ready",
        "resp_stream_valid",
        "resp_stream_payload",
        "actuator_cmd_valid",
        "actuator_cmd_out",
        "fault_irq"
      ],
      "must_receive": [
        "clk",
        "rst_n",
        "host_reg_addr",
        "host_reg_wdata",
        "host_reg_be",
        "host_reg_valid",
        "host_reg_write",
        "cmd_stream_valid",
        "cmd_stream_payload",
        "resp_stream_ready"
      ],
      "must_not_drive": [
        "host_reg_addr",
        "host_reg_wdata",
        "host_reg_be",
        "host_reg_valid",
        "host_reg_write",
        "cmd_stream_valid",
        "cmd_stream_payload",
        "resp_stream_ready"
      ],
      "reset_behavior": "On reset deassertion release, all registers and state machine state return to safe defaults. Actuator command validity is deasserted and actuator_cmd_out is held at a benign encoded value while invalid. Sticky faults clear on reset. Ready/valid outputs return to idle-safe values. No command is acknowledged during reset or until the interface is fully initialized.",
      "behavior_rules": [
        "A command is accepted only on a valid/ready handshake, when sequence number is newer than the last accepted sequence, and when the command age/timestamp is within the configured watchdog window.",
        "If a command is invalid, stale, timed out, or out of sequence, it must not be acknowledged as accepted.",
        "Requested actuator values are clamped to configured minimum and maximum bounds before becoming applied outputs.",
        "Slew limiting is applied against the last applied command using the configured slew limit register.",
        "The design may hold actuator output validity low rather than substituting a fallback command on fault or reset.",
        "Sticky fault bits are writable-one-to-clear or clearable through dedicated clear control fields and otherwise remain latched.",
        "Reads return live status and shadowed applied/accepted command values from the register map.",
        "The design never emits an unclamped actuator command to actuator outputs."
      ],
      "rtl_output_file": "adaptive_aero_control_top.v"
    },
