        "functionality": "Consumes compact command words and produces validated, bounded actuator commands and response metadata. The module is responsible for handshake qualification, age/timeout evaluation, sequence ordering, clamp and slew enforcement, sticky-fault generation, and shadow updates that are read by software. Invalid or stale commands are rejected, not accepted, and do not drive a valid actuator command.",
        "responsibilities": [
          "Validate command sequence freshness and age.",
          "Enforce watchdog timeout based on configured threshold.",
          "Clamp requested actuator setpoints to configured min/max.",
          "Apply slew limiting relative to the last applied command.",
          "Assert response metadata for accept/reject and fault reasons.",
          "Drive fault interrupt when any sticky or active fault condition occurs.",
          "Expose shadowed last accepted command, applied command, error code, and heartbeat timestamp."
        ],
