        "reset_behavior": "Returns to safe invalid state on reset, deasserting actuator command validity and clearing shadow state and sticky faults. No command can be accepted until reset release and reinitialization complete.",
        "behavior_rules": [
          "A command may only be accepted when valid/ready handshake completes.",
          "Sequence numbers must be strictly newer than the last accepted sequence.",
          "Freshness must be checked using explicit timestamp/age or cycle delta.",
          "Commands outside configured bounds must be clamped, with range_violation set if any clamping occurs.",
          "Slew limiting must be based on the last applied value and the configured slew limit.",
          "On invalid or stale commands, the module may not assert actuator_cmd_valid.",
          "Sticky faults may clear only via explicit software clear control.",
          "Response payload must report accept/reject, applied/clamped setpoint, fault code, and freshness/timeout flags.",
          "No fallback command is substituted; invalid conditions simply inhibit actuator validity."
        ],
